<LessonLayout title="Catechist's Guide &mdash; The Sources of Prayer" cic="CCC 2590-2649" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For class preparation and delivery. For the catechist's use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> Christian prayer draws from living sources: the Word of God, Tradition, the Liturgy, and daily life.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Discover Scripture as the primary source of prayer.</li>
<li>Know the method of Lectio Divina.</li>
<li>Value the Liturgy as the prayer of the Church.</li>
<li>Learn from the saints as masters of prayer.</li>
<li>Integrate prayer into daily life.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> &laquo;Your word is a lamp to my feet and a light to my path&raquo; (Ps 119:105)</p>
<p><strong>CCC references:</strong> 2590-2649</p>

</section>

